envelope "Attleboro research flow step with frozen sampled slope"

Guideline
    The research OpenPLC simulator updates q by q + 0.4*(target-q)
    every 0.1 seconds. This finite ODE phase freezes the sampled q0 in
    the slope, so its exact endpoint matches that update before the
    simulator's q<0.01 snap-to-zero. It proves only 0<=q<=10 in this
    research fixture, not Attleboro site hydraulics or minimum service.

Definitions
    Definitions
    End.

    ProgramVariables
        Real q; Real q0; Real target; Real t;
    End.

precondition
    0 <= q & q <= 10 & (target = 0 | target = 10)

postcondition
    0 <= q & q <= 10 & t = 1/10

game
    {
        q0 := q;
        t := 0;
        flow_ode: {
            q' = 4*(target-q0),
            t' = 1
            & t <= 1/10
        };
        ? t >= 1/10;
    }
